The condition you're seeing:

Message:
Error while reconciling: some StorageClasses were skipped while waiting for pre-requisites to be met:
[ocs-storagecluster-cephfs, ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd]

does not indicate the root problem. It simply means the ODF operator is waiting because the Ceph cluster is not ready.

From the information you've already shared:

✅ MONs are running

✅ MGR is running

✅ MDS is running

❌ OSDs = 0

❌ No rook-ceph-osd pods exist

❌ Ceph reports OSD count 0 < osd_pool_default_size 3


Because there are no OSDs, the Ceph pools cannot become active, so the ODF operator skips creating the ocs-storagecluster-ceph-rbd and ocs-storagecluster-cephfs StorageClasses until the prerequisites are met.

The real issue is still: Why weren't any OSDs created?

To answer that, we need the outputs of these commands:

oc describe localvolumeset local-volume -n openshift-local-storage

oc get localvolumediscoveryresult -n openshift-local-storage -o yaml

oc get pv

oc logs deploy/rook-ceph-operator -n openshift-storage --tail=300

The LocalVolumeSet and LocalVolumeDiscoveryResult will tell us whether suitable disks were discovered, and the Rook operator logs will usually contain the exact reason OSD creation failed (for example, disks already contain partitions/LVM, no eligible devices match the filter, or another provisioning error).

At this point, the StorageClass message is expected behavior—the investigation should focus on why OSD creation failed.
